--TEST--
`Core\Router\Match::attribute<T>()` does not compile where one routed method has two attributes of the declaration `T` names: `E0728` names the method, and a method with one is not reported — `rule:routing/a-match-reads-an-attribute-as-data`
--FILE--
<?nvs
repeatable attribute Limit on method { limit: int, label?: string }

class Shop {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/shop", method: Core\Http\Method::Get)]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    #[Limit(limit: 10)]
    #[Limit(limit: 20, label: "high")]
    public function index(): void {}

    #[Core\Route(path: "/cart", method: Core\Http\Method::Get)]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    #[Limit(limit: 5)]
    public function cart(): void {}
}

?Core\Router\Match $shop = Core\Router::match(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/shop");
var $limit = $shop?->attribute<Limit>();
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0728]: `Shop::index` has 2 `Limit` attributes
   --> case.nvs:18:14
   |
18 | var $limit = $shop?->attribute<Limit>();
   |              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `attribute` returns at most one
   = help: read `Shop::index` with `Core\Attributes::all<T>(…)`, which returns every one

error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
